ore pickup; parcel never left the dock\n2026-09-18T20:05:51Z DEBUG heartbeat worker=w34 ok\n2026-09-18T19:54:14Z DEBUG heartbeat worker=w9 ok\n2026-09-17T00:02:08Z DEBUG heartbeat worker=w82 ok\n2026-09-18T10:55:07Z INFO  dispatch id=SHP-1017 carrier=dhl wt=33.79kg dest=\"Bremen\"\n2026-09-18T10:35:26Z DEBUG heartbeat worker=w35 ok\n2026-09-18T04:02:33Z DEBUG gc pause 91ms\n2026-09-20T20:25:58Z DEBUG heartbeat worker=w71 ok\n2026-09-15T21:31:18Z INFO  queue depth=91\n2026-09-18T07:21:12Z INFO  queue depth=91\n2026-09-18T09:07:10Z INFO  dispatch id=SHP-1018 carrier=ups wt=1.47kg dest=\"Turin\"\n\n== shift notes ==\n- SHP-1019 went out with DPD to Bremen on 2026-09-18, 23.9 kg.\n- 2026-09-18: handed SHP-1020 (19.34 kg, destination Madrid) to the DPD driver.\n- Dispatched SHP-1021 on 2026-09-19 -> Valencia. Carrier: dpd. Weight 19.52 kg.\n- SHP-1022 went out with ups to Bologna on 2026-09-19, 34.02 kg.\n- 2026-09-19: handed SHP-1023 (4.4 kg, destination Ghent) to the DPD driver.\n- Customer in Lyon called about late delivery; told them we would check tomorrow.\n- Dispatched SHP-1024 on 2026-09-19 -> Utrecht. Carrier: DPD. Weight 23.5 kg.\n- SHP-1025 went out with FedEx to Leipzig on 2026-09-20, 7.33 kg.\n- 2026-09-20: handed SHP-1026 (22.14 kg, destination Bologna) to the DPD driver.\n- Planned for next week: SHP-1098 via DHL to Lyon, about 9.5 kg. Not booked yet.\n- Dispatched SHP-1027 on 2026-09-20 -> Porto. Carrier: ups. Weight 5.33 kg.\n- SHP-1028 went out with DPD to Lyon on 2026-09-20, 47.27 kg.\n- Reminder: re-tape pallets before the afternoon pickup.\n- 2026-09-21: handed SHP-1029 (29.0 kg, destination Lisbon) to the DHL Express driver.\n- Dispatched SHP-1030 on 2026-09-21 -> Madrid. Carrier: DPD. Weight 45.6 kg.\n\n== whiteboard table ==\n| id | date | carrier | weight | destination |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SHP-1031 | 2026-09-21 | dpd | 7.47 kg | Turin |\n| SHP-1032 | 2026-09-21 | FedEx Ground | 6.25 kg | Brno |\n| SHP-1033 | 2026-09-22 | ups | 15.2 kg | Seville |\n| SHP-1034 | 2026-09-22 | fedex | 13.0 kg | Lisbon |\n| SHP-1035 | 2026-09-22 | dpd | 7.4 kg | Bremen |\n| SHP-1036 | 2026-09-22 | dhl | 40.64 kg | Lyon |\n\n== legacy terminal (dates in this section are DD/MM/YYYY) ==\nDSP 23/09/2026 SHP-1037 FEDEX            25.75 KG  TO GHENT\n2026-09-23T01:11:12Z WARN  label printer p40 low on paper\nDSP 23/09/2026 SHP-1038 DPD            1,250.5 KG  TO NANTES\n2026-09-23T16:48:13Z WARN  label printer p38 low on paper\nDSP 23/09/2026 SHP-1039 UPS               35.2 KG  TO UTRECHT\n2026-09-23T16:43:11Z INFO  sync inventory batch=35 rows=0\nDSP 23/09/2026 SHP-1040 UPS               9.62 KG  TO BRNO\n2026-09-23T00:16:02Z WARN  label printer p2 low on paper\n\nend of export\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re, json, hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime\nsrc = Path('dispatch_log.txt')\nbefore = hashlib.sha256(src.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\ntext = src.read_text()\nvoided = set(re.findall(r'dispatch id=(SHP-\\\\d+) VOIDED', text))\nrecords = {}\ndef add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest):\n    if id in voided:\n        return\n    record = dict(id=id, date=date, carrier=carrier.split()[0].lower(), weight_kg=float(weight.replace(',', '')), dest=dest.title())\n    if id in records:\n        assert records[id] == record, id\n    records[id] = record\njoined = re.sub(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\s*', '', text)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'(\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2})T\\\\S+ INFO\\\\s+dispatch id=(SHP-\\\\d+) carrier=(.*?) wt=([\\\\d.]+)kg dest=\\\"([\"'^\"]+)\"'\"', joined):\n    date, id, carrier, weight, dest = m.groups()\n    add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'- (SHP-\\\\d+) went out with (.*?) to (.*?) on (\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}), ([\\\\d.]+) kg\\\\.', text):\n    id, carrier, dest, date, weight = m.groups()\n    add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'- (\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}): handed (SHP-\\\\d+) \\\\(([\\\\d.]+) kg, destination ([\"'^)]+)'\"\\\\) to the (.*?) driver\\\\.', text):\n    date, id, weight, dest, carrier = m.groups()\n    add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'- Dispatched (SHP-\\\\d+) on (\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}) -> (.*?)\\\\. Carrier: (.*?)\\\\. Weight ([\\\\d.]+) kg\\\\.', text):\n    id, date, dest, carrier, weight = m.groups()\n    add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest)\nfor line in text.splitlines():\n    if line.startswith('| SHP-'):\n        id, date, carrier, weight, dest = [v.strip() for v in line.strip('|').split('|')]\n        add(id, date, carrier, weight.removesuffix(' kg'), dest)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'\"'^DSP ('\"\\\\d{2}/\\\\d{2}/\\\\d{4}) (SHP-\\\\d+) (\\\\w+)\\\\s+([\\\\d,.]+) KG\\\\s+TO (.+)\"'$'\"', text, re.M):\n    date, id, carrier, weight, dest = m.groups()\n    add(id, datetime.strptime(date, '%d/%m/%Y').strftime('%Y-%m-%d'), carrier, weight, dest)\nresult = sorted(records.values(), key=lambda r: r['id'])\nassert set(records) == {f'SHP-{i}' for i in range(1001, 1041)}\nfor r in result:\n    assert set(r) == {'id', 'date', 'carrier', 'weight_kg', 'dest'}\n    assert r['carrier'] in {'dhl', 'ups', 'fedex', 'dpd'}\n    datetime.strptime(r['date'], '%Y-%m-%d')\nPath('records.json').write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2) + '\\\\n')\nassert json.loads(Path('records.json').read_text()) == result\nassert hashlib.sha256(src.read_bytes()).hexdigest() == before\nprint(f'{len(result)} records written and verified.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re, json, hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime\nsrc = Path('dispatch_log.txt')\nbefore = hashlib.sha256(src.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\ntext = src.read_text()\nvoided = set(re.findall(r'dispatch id=(SHP-\\\\d+) VOIDED', text))\nrecords = {}\ndef add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest):\n    if id in voided:\n        return\n    record = dict(id=id, date=date, carrier=carrier.split()[0].lower(), weight_kg=float(weight.replace(',', '')), dest=dest.title())\n    if id in records:\n        assert records[id] == record, id\n    records[id] = record\njoined = re.sub(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\s*', '', text)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'(\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2})T\\\\S+ INFO\\\\s+dispatch id=(SHP-\\\\d+) carrier=(.*?) wt=([\\\\d.]+)kg dest=\\\"([\"'^\"]+)\"'\"', joined):\n    date, id, carrier, weight, dest = m.groups()\n    add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'- (SHP-\\\\d+) went out with (.*?) to (.*?) on (\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}), ([\\\\d.]+) kg\\\\.', text):\n    id, carrier, dest, date, weight = m.groups()\n    add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'- (\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}): handed (SHP-\\\\d+) \\\\(([\\\\d.]+) kg, destination ([\"'^)]+)'\"\\\\) to the (.*?) driver\\\\.', text):\n    date, id, weight, dest, carrier = m.groups()\n    add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'- Dispatched (SHP-\\\\d+) on (\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}) -> (.*?)\\\\. Carrier: (.*?)\\\\. Weight ([\\\\d.]+) kg\\\\.', text):\n    id, date, dest, carrier, weight = m.groups()\n    add(id, date, carrier, weight, dest)\nfor line in text.splitlines():\n    if line.startswith('| SHP-'):\n        id, date, carrier, weight, dest = [v.strip() for v in line.strip('|').split('|')]\n        add(id, date, carrier, weight.removesuffix(' kg'), dest)\nfor m in re.finditer(r'\"'^DSP ('\"\\\\d{2}/\\\\d{2}/\\\\d{4}) (SHP-\\\\d+) (\\\\w+)\\\\s+([\\\\d,.]+) KG\\\\s+TO (.+)\"'$'\"', text, re.M):\n    date, id, carrier, weight, dest = m.groups()\n    add(id, datetime.strptime(date, '%d/%m/%Y').strftime('%Y-%m-%d'), carrier, weight, dest)\nresult = sorted(records.values(), key=lambda r: r['id'])\nassert set(records) == {f'SHP-{i}' for i in range(1001, 1041)}\nfor r in result:\n    assert set(r) == {'id', 'date', 'carrier', 'weight_kg', 'dest'}\n    assert r['carrier'] in {'dhl', 'ups', 'fedex', 'dpd'}\n    datetime.strptime(r['date'], '%Y-%m-%d')\nPath('records.json').write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2) + '\\\\n')\nassert json.loads(Path('records.json').read_text()) == result\nassert hashlib.sha256(src.read_bytes()).hexdigest() == before\nprint(f'{len(result)} records written and verified.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"40 records written and verified.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
